    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "86b7cdaedaf8d9360f4b52abc0da0638",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"two-loop-photon-renormalization-and-ibp\">Two-loop photon renormalization and IBP</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/qed_renormalization.py\">One-loop QED</a> \u00b7\n<a href=\"/?file=hep/electron_two_loop.py\">Two-loop electron</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generate all three massless QED photon self-energy diagrams in a\n<strong>symbolic covariant gauge</strong>, retain both open Lorentz indices, and\nreduce their UV expansion with native IBP. Calculate the four one-loop\ncounterterm insertions on a generated photon bubble, then determine\nthe two-loop field and auxiliary-mass counterterms.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This reproduces the complete tensor poles and renormalization constants\nof the <a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QED/TwoLoops/Renormalization-GaGa\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">FeynCalc reference</a>.\nWe use <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D=4-2\\epsilon||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(a_4=e^2/(16\\pi^2)||)</marimo-tex> and\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(T^{\\mu\\nu}=p^2g^{\\mu\\nu}-p^\\mu p^\\nu||)</marimo-tex>.\nBoth tensor coefficients are checked independently. Adjust the gauge,\nflavor count and auxiliary mass below to see the cancellation.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
